  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-23T23:43:07.285Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, there used to be a way with the API where you were able to see into specific lobbies playerlist if you had the full InstanceID. Some non-vrchat applications took advantage of this and let players look into lobbies of friends, friends+ and public lobbies. However, today it seems that API endpoint was closed off. So, I guess this is the time where we ask this to become a feature. \nCould we please have a way to display a playerlist of worlds we are able to join? This would be extremely useful for people who just want to know if a group of friends are all in a single lobby, or if the persons just alone sitting afk in a world. It gets extremely frustrating not being able to have a remote lobby playerlist if you just want to find friends to spend time with rather then world hopping for 20mins before finding a suitable lobby.",
